 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Gas oven took ages to light tonight then went WHOOMPH and now the kitchen smells really strongly of gas even though I've turned it off. Is it safe to try again?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "⚠ Stop using this appliance\nIf you can smell gas, treat it as an emergency: don't turn any switches on or off and no naked flames. Turn the gas off at the meter if you safely can, open doors and windows, and leave if the smell is strong. Call the National Gas Emergency line on 0800 111 999."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok I'm really panicking, the smell is still strong. The meter box is outside by the front door, should I turn it off there? I'm renting and I can't get hold of the landlord tonight. Also I've got a slight headache and no CO alarm."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "⚠ Stop using this appliance\nGiven you have a strong smell of gas and are feeling unwell (headache), this is a serious emergency. Do not try to use the oven again or investigate it yourself. Once the gas is isolated, leave the property immediately and call the National Gas Emergency line on 0800 111 999 from outside. Tell them you suspect a leak and are feeling symptoms of gas exposure."
  }
 ],
